statement:
For a site $\mathcal{C}$ and arrow $f:U\to V$, the induced functor $j_{U/V}:\mathcal{C}/U\to\mathcal{C}/V$ sends $(X\to U)$ to $(X\to U\to V)$. It is a continuous and cocontinuous morphism of sites and induces the corresponding morphism of topoi, with $j_U=j_V\circ j_{U/V}$ on sites and topoi.

